WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.670
Picture a culture in which
every cell divides in two,

2
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.210
generation after generation.

3
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:11.990
After 12 generations, every
starting cell has become 4096.

4
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.470
Microbe numbers can span
from a hundred to a billion:

5
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.300
many powers of ten.

6
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.590
So how do you count them, and how
do you graph numbers that huge?

7
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:26.190
In this mission, you'll see why an ordinary
axis squashes the early points flat

8
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:27.520
against zero.

9
00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:30.740
Then you'll redraw the
same data on a log scale,

10
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:33.420
and follow a culture through its lag, log,

11
00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:35.850
stationary and death phases.

12
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.030
Your mission: find out
how to count bacteria,

13
00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:40.670
and how to graph their growth.
